{:title "Multi-Pass Code Review"
 :slug "review-learns-prometheus"
 :description "Build a workflow that reviews code through multiple providers and compares results"
 :date "2026-04-14"
 :duration "15min"
 :steps
 [{:heading "Create the review workflow"
   :body [[:p "Start by creating a workflow that runs a code review through multiple providers. Create " [:code ".glitch/workflows/review-compare.glitch"] ":"]
          [:code {:lang "clojure"} "(workflow \"review-compare\"\n  :description \"Multi-pass review across providers\"\n\n  (step \"diff\"\n    (run \"git diff main...HEAD\"))\n\n  (step \"review-local\"\n    (llm :provider \"lmstudio\" :model \"qwen3-8b\"\n      :prompt ```\n        Review this diff for bugs, security issues, and style problems.\n        Be specific -- cite line numbers and suggest fixes.\n        ~(ref \"diff\")\n        ```))\n\n  (step \"review-copilot\"\n    (llm :provider \"copilot\"\n      :prompt ```\n        Review this diff for bugs, security issues, and style problems.\n        Be specific -- cite line numbers and suggest fixes.\n        ~(ref \"diff\")\n        ```)))"]]}
  {:heading "Add a grading step"
   :body [[:p "Add a neutral judge that scores each review. Use a local model so grading stays fast and free:"]
          [:code {:lang "clojure"} "  (step \"grade\"\n    (llm :provider \"lmstudio\" :model \"qwen3-8b\"\n      :prompt ```\n        You are a code review evaluator. Score each review 1-10 on:\n        - Completeness: did it catch real issues?\n        - Specificity: did it cite lines and suggest fixes?\n        - Accuracy: are the suggestions correct?\n\n        --- LOCAL REVIEW ---\n        ~(ref \"review-local\")\n\n        --- COPILOT REVIEW ---\n        ~(ref \"review-copilot\")\n\n        Output:\n        WINNER: <variant>\n        SCORES: local=N copilot=N\n        REASON: <one sentence>\n        ```))"]]}
  {:heading "Run the comparison"
   :body [[:p "Run your workflow against a branch with changes:"]
          [:code {:lang "bash"} "glitch run .glitch/workflows/review-compare.glitch"]
          [:p "You will see step-by-step progress on stderr and the final graded output on stdout."]]}
  {:heading "Add a third provider"
   :body [[:p "Add Claude as a third branch. Insert this step after " [:code "review-copilot"] ":"]
          [:code {:lang "clojure"} "  (step \"review-claude\"\n    (llm :provider \"claude\"\n      :prompt ```\n        Review this diff for bugs, security issues, and style problems.\n        Be specific -- cite line numbers and suggest fixes.\n        ~(ref \"diff\")\n        ```))"]
          [:p "Update the grading step prompt to include all three reviews and add Claude to the output format."]]}
  {:heading "Save and iterate"
   :body [[:p "Add a save step at the end to keep results for later comparison:"]
          [:code {:lang "clojure"} "  (step \"save\"\n    (save \"results/review-comparison.md\" (ref \"grade\")))"]
          [:p "Run this across multiple PRs to build intuition for which provider gives you the best reviews for your codebase. Pin the grader model so scores stay comparable across runs."]]}]}
